sub('The output is the probability vector (1−p,p), not an assumed output softmax. No LayerNorm or unpriced external division is used.', 'The ideal output is the probability vector (1−p,p), not an assumed output softmax. A backend with a final numerical error must additionally execute the explicitly costed post-error saturation and preserve the exact complement, or analyze separate saturation/normalization errors. The added saturation is one scalar clip operation or one further ReLU block if counted as a neural layer. No LayerNorm or unpriced external division is used.')
sub('except final probability error ≤ζ.', 'except pre-saturation final scalar error ≤ζ, followed by exact final saturation and exact complement.')
sub('A final numerical output-rounding error', 'A final numerical output-rounding error') if False else None
sub('The first condition also implies e≤u/4.', 'The first condition also implies e≤u/4. Under approximate rather than exact final saturation, add its separately bounded ξ to the final risk; independent coordinate rounding must not be silently treated as exact normalization.')
sub('The comparator: an ordinary same-history streaming add-one counter tracks all four row/successor counts before seeing the terminal pair, O(N) updates, O(log N) bits per fixed-number counter plus a paid final division.', 'The comparator: an ordinary same-history streaming add-one counter tracks all four row/successor counts; on seeing X_N it performs the last transition update, forms S_N, and then reads the appropriate row. It requires O(N) updates, O(log N) bits per fixed-number counter plus a paid final division.') if 'The comparator: an ordinary' in s else None
sub('Comparator: an ordinary same-history streaming add-one counter tracks all four row/successor counts before seeing the terminal pair, O(N) updates, O(log N) bits per fixed-number counter plus a paid final division.', 'Comparator: an ordinary same-history streaming add-one counter tracks all four row/successor counts; on seeing X_N it performs the last transition update, forms S_N, and then reads the appropriate row. It requires O(N) updates, O(log N) bits per fixed-number counter plus a paid final division.')
sub('Our construction pays two extra heads and O(K)-width arithmetic, and does not establish an efficiency improvement, a necessary depth, or an N–L lower bound.', 'Compared with a direct-q network sharing the same two-copy-head block, this construction adds one uniform head plus selection and O(K)-width arithmetic; in total it uses four head instances across the two attention blocks. Against a streaming counter it uses four head instances where the counter uses none. It establishes no efficiency improvement, necessary depth or N–L lower bound.')
sub('O(N) token-state storage;', 'O(N) token-state storage, excluding any training/backpropagation retention of O(NK) intermediate FFN activations;')
sub('The stochastic and generic perturbation proof received a distinct agent check; finite spline and full architecture remain unreviewed.', 'One distinct reviewer checked the conditional probability and generic perturbation proof. A second distinct adversarial reviewer checked the structured masks, seven-block schedule, spline inequalities and resource account; it also identified the K=1 zero-count example. These checks do not supply dense-causal compilation, complete floating-point error, statistical novelty, formal verification or complete proof-review acceptance. The reviewers separately confirmed the corrected final-saturation and Q/K/V notes.')
sub('No complete proof-review procedure was run;', 'R011 already proves an unconditional actual-terminal add-one upper bound for all homogeneous order-2 sources even without mixing, and SM001 already uses reverse conditioning under its stronger two-step π-minorization; this rare-row conditional bound and the two-step common-atom certificate are a distinct mathematical scope but not a novelty certificate. See scope_antecedents_addendum_v1.html for provenance. No complete proof-review procedure was run;')
